package com.kingdomlife.app.success;

import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;

public class Chapter02GoodSuccessAndBadSuccess {

    public static final String TITLE = "Good Success and Bad Success";

    public static final String SUBTITLE =
            "Understanding the Difference Between Success That Pleases God and Success That Does Not";

    public static final List<String> PAGES = Arrays.asList(

            // PAGE 1
            "2.1 INTRODUCTION\n\n" +
            "Success is something many people desire. People work hard, make plans, pursue opportunities and set goals because they want to achieve something meaningful in life.\n\n" +
            "However, an important question must be considered: Is every kind of success good?\n\n" +
            "The answer is no. Although success is generally associated with achievement and progress, the way a person achieves success and the things pursued in the process matter greatly.\n\n" +
            "A person may become wealthy but lack integrity. Another may become popular but use that popularity to influence others negatively. Someone may achieve a position of authority but use that position to exploit people.\n\n" +
            "These examples remind us that achievement alone does not determine whether success is good.\n\n" +
            "In this chapter, we will examine good success and bad success, their differences, their consequences and the principles that should guide our pursuit of success.\n\n" +
            "Our desire should not simply be to succeed, but to experience success that is meaningful, beneficial and consistent with God's principles.",

            // PAGE 2
            "2.2 WHAT IS GOOD SUCCESS?\n\n" +
            "Good success is success achieved and maintained through principles that are pleasing to God. It involves making progress in life without abandoning righteousness, integrity, wisdom and love for others.\n\n" +
            "Good success is not limited to financial achievements or public recognition. It includes spiritual growth, good character, meaningful relationships, responsible living and fulfilling the purposes God has placed before us.\n\n" +
            "Joshua 1:8 (KJV) teaches the importance of meditating on God's Word and observing to do according to what is written in it. The passage connects obedience to God's Word with having a prosperous way and good success.\n\n" +
            "This teaches us that God's principles should influence the decisions we make and the goals we pursue.\n\n" +
            "Good success does not mean that a person will never encounter difficulties. It means that the person continues to pursue what is right, trusting God and applying wisdom even when the journey becomes challenging.\n\n" +
            "A student who studies diligently and remains honest, a businessperson who treats customers fairly, and a leader who serves responsibly are examples of people pursuing success through good principles.",

            // PAGE 3
            "2.3 WHAT IS BAD SUCCESS?\n\n" +
            "Bad success refers to achievement pursued or maintained through wrong principles, harmful behaviour or actions that oppose what is right.\n\n" +
            "It is possible for someone to achieve a desired result while using dishonesty, manipulation, exploitation or injustice. Such achievement may attract admiration from people, but it does not make the method right.\n\n" +
            "For example, a person may obtain good examination results through cheating. Although the result may appear successful, the method used is dishonest and does not represent good success.\n\n" +
            "Another person may become wealthy through fraud or by taking advantage of others. The money gained does not make the actions acceptable.\n\n" +
            "Proverbs 10:2 (KJV) reminds us that treasures of wickedness do not profit, while righteousness delivers from death.\n\n" +
            "Bad success may sometimes appear attractive because its immediate rewards are visible. However, we must consider the character, consequences and methods behind every achievement.\n\n" +
            "The important lesson is that we should never allow the desire to achieve something to make us abandon what is right.",

            // PAGE 4
            "2.4 THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN GOOD SUCCESS AND BAD SUCCESS\n\n" +
            "The difference between good success and bad success is not simply the amount of money earned, the position occupied or the level of recognition received. It is also found in the principles and behaviour behind the achievement.\n\n" +
            "Good success values integrity, while bad success may depend on dishonesty.\n\n" +
            "Good success considers the welfare of others, while bad success may involve using people for personal advantage.\n\n" +
            "Good success encourages responsible progress, while bad success may pursue immediate rewards without considering the consequences.\n\n" +
            "Good success seeks to honour God, while bad success places personal ambition above righteousness.\n\n" +
            "Good success recognises that character matters, while bad success may concentrate only on outward appearance and recognition.\n\n" +
            "Proverbs 22:1 (KJV) teaches that a good name is rather to be chosen than great riches, and loving favour rather than silver and gold.\n\n" +
            "This reminds us that reputation, character and integrity are valuable. We should not exchange them for achievements that cannot give us lasting fulfilment.",

            // PAGE 5
            "2.5 BIBLICAL EXAMPLE: JOSEPH AND INTEGRITY\n\n" +
            "Joseph's experience in Egypt provides an important lesson about good success.\n\n" +
            "After being sold by his brothers, Joseph found himself serving in Potiphar's house. Despite his difficult circumstances, he remained responsible and faithful in his duties.\n\n" +
            "When Potiphar's wife attempted to persuade him to do what was wrong, Joseph refused. He understood that committing such an act would be a sin against God.\n\n" +
            "Genesis 39:9 (KJV) records Joseph's response, showing that he recognised the seriousness of the temptation and refused to do such wickedness.\n\n" +
            "Joseph suffered consequences for doing what was right and was eventually imprisoned. Yet he did not abandon his principles.\n\n" +
            "Later, God gave him favour and wisdom, and he was elevated to a position of great responsibility in Egypt.\n\n" +
            "Joseph's story teaches us that good success requires integrity even when doing the right thing is difficult. We should not sacrifice our values simply because we want quick progress.",

            // PAGE 6
            "2.6 BIBLICAL WARNING: THE RICH FOOL\n\n" +
            "In Luke 12:16–21, Jesus told a parable about a rich man whose land produced plentifully.\n\n" +
            "The man became concerned about where to store his increasing harvest. He decided to pull down his barns and build greater ones so that he could store all his goods.\n\n" +
            "He then planned to enjoy his wealth and live comfortably for many years. However, God called him a fool because his life would be required of him that night.\n\n" +
            "The problem in the parable was not simply that the man had possessions. Rather, he placed his confidence in his earthly wealth and failed to become rich towards God.\n\n" +
            "Luke 12:21 (KJV) teaches that this is the condition of someone who lays up treasure for himself but is not rich towards God.\n\n" +
            "This parable reminds us that material achievement alone is not the highest measure of success.\n\n" +
            "We should plan responsibly, work diligently and manage our resources wisely, while remembering that our relationship with God and the condition of our hearts are important.",

            // PAGE 7
            "2.7 THE DANGER OF PURSUING SUCCESS WITHOUT PRINCIPLES\n\n" +
            "When people become too focused on achieving their goals, they may begin to believe that any method is acceptable as long as the desired result is obtained.\n\n" +
            "This way of thinking can lead to dishonesty, unhealthy competition, pride, exploitation and the neglect of important responsibilities.\n\n" +
            "A student may become so concerned about grades that the student chooses cheating instead of honest preparation. A businessperson may become so interested in profit that fairness and honesty are ignored. A person seeking recognition may begin to look down on others.\n\n" +
            "These actions can damage character and relationships.\n\n" +
            "Mark 8:36 (KJV) asks what it profits a person to gain the whole world and lose his own soul.\n\n" +
            "This question challenges us to examine what we are pursuing and what we may be sacrificing along the way.\n\n" +
            "Our goals should never become more important to us than our relationship with God, our character and our responsibility towards others.",

            // PAGE 8
            "2.8 CAN A PERSON HAVE WEALTH AND STILL EXPERIENCE GOOD SUCCESS?\n\n" +
            "Yes. Wealth itself is not automatically bad, and poverty is not automatically a sign of righteousness.\n\n" +
            "The important questions include how wealth is obtained, how it is managed and whether it is used responsibly.\n\n" +
            "A person can work diligently, develop useful skills, run an honest business, save wisely and become financially successful while maintaining good character.\n\n" +
            "The Bible encourages diligence and responsible stewardship. Proverbs 21:5 (KJV) teaches that the thoughts of the diligent tend only to plenteousness, while haste tends to want.\n\n" +
            "First Timothy 6:17–19 also gives instructions concerning those who are rich in this world. They should not be proud or place their trust in uncertain riches, but in the living God. They are also encouraged to be rich in good works and ready to distribute.\n\n" +
            "Therefore, financial progress should be accompanied by humility, generosity and responsibility.\n\n" +
            "Good success is not measured only by what we possess, but also by how faithfully and wisely we live.",

            // PAGE 9
            "2.9 HOW TO PURSUE GOOD SUCCESS\n\n" +
            "There are practical principles that can help us pursue good success.\n\n" +
            "1. Put God first. Let your relationship with God influence your goals and decisions.\n\n" +
            "2. Study and apply God's Word. Do not merely read Scripture; seek to practise its teachings.\n\n" +
            "3. Maintain integrity. Be truthful and responsible, even when dishonesty appears easier.\n\n" +
            "4. Work diligently. Develop your abilities and give proper attention to your responsibilities.\n\n" +
            "5. Seek wisdom. Think carefully before making decisions and learn from trustworthy guidance.\n\n" +
            "6. Treat people well. Do not use others as stepping stones for personal advancement.\n\n" +
            "7. Remain humble. Recognise that achievements should not make you proud or disrespectful.\n\n" +
            "8. Learn from mistakes. When you make a wrong decision, acknowledge it, make necessary corrections and continue growing.\n\n" +
            "These principles help us pursue meaningful progress without abandoning the values that should guide our lives.",

            // PAGE 10
            "2.10 SUCCESS THAT BENEFITS OTHERS\n\n" +
            "Good success should not be centred entirely on personal advantage. It should also create opportunities to contribute positively to the lives of others.\n\n" +
            "A person who gains knowledge can use it to teach and encourage others. Someone who develops leadership abilities can serve responsibly. A person who becomes financially stable may be able to support people in need.\n\n" +
            "The abilities, opportunities and resources we receive can become instruments through which we make meaningful contributions.\n\n" +
            "Galatians 6:10 (KJV) encourages us to do good unto all men, especially those who are of the household of faith.\n\n" +
            "This does not mean that we must solve every problem around us or neglect our own responsibilities. It means that our progress should not make us selfish or indifferent to the needs of others.\n\n" +
            "A successful life should have room for kindness, service, encouragement and generosity.",

            // PAGE 11
            "2.11 CHOOSING THE RIGHT KIND OF SUCCESS\n\n" +
            "Every person must make decisions about the kind of life they want to build. These decisions are influenced by personal goals, family expectations, society, opportunities and the examples we observe around us.\n\n" +
            "However, we must not allow pressure from other people to determine our values.\n\n" +
            "Some people may encourage us to pursue achievements without considering whether the methods are right. Others may measure success only through wealth, popularity, appearance or social position.\n\n" +
            "We should learn to examine our goals in the light of God's Word.\n\n" +
            "Before pursuing an opportunity, consider whether it requires dishonesty, whether it will harm others, whether it conflicts with your responsibilities and whether it encourages you to abandon your values.\n\n" +
            "Proverbs 3:5–6 (KJV) teaches us to trust in the LORD with all our heart, not lean on our own understanding, acknowledge Him in all our ways and allow Him to direct our paths.\n\n" +
            "Choosing good success requires more than ambition. It requires the willingness to allow God to guide our decisions.",

            // PAGE 12
            "2.12 CONCLUSION: LET YOUR SUCCESS BE GOOD SUCCESS\n\n" +
            "As we pursue progress in life, we must remember that the destination is not the only thing that matters. The journey, the methods we use and the character we develop are equally important.\n\n" +
            "Good success is not about appearing successful before people while neglecting what truly matters. It is about growing, achieving meaningful goals and remaining faithful to the principles of God.\n\n" +
            "We should desire progress in our spiritual lives, education, relationships, family responsibilities, careers, service and other areas of life. In every area, integrity and godly wisdom should remain part of our foundation.\n\n" +
            "Let us not pursue achievements at the expense of our character. Let us not allow temporary rewards to make us abandon lasting values.\n\n" +
            "May our ambitions be guided by God's Word, our actions reflect righteousness and our achievements become a blessing rather than a source of harm.\n\n" +
            "The goal is not merely to succeed. The goal is to experience good success.",

            // REFLECTION
            "CHAPTER REFLECTION\n\n" +
            "1. How would you explain the difference between good success and bad success?\n\n" +
            "2. Can someone achieve something impressive through dishonest methods? Why does that matter?\n\n" +
            "3. What lesson can you learn from Joseph's decision to maintain his integrity?\n\n" +
            "4. What does the parable of the rich fool teach about the danger of trusting only in material possessions?\n\n" +
            "5. Which values should guide your pursuit of success?\n\n" +
            "6. How can your achievements become a blessing to other people?\n\n" +
            "7. Is there any goal you need to reconsider so that it agrees with God's principles?",

            // KEY LESSONS
            "KEY LESSONS TO REMEMBER\n\n" +
            "• Not every achievement represents good success.\n\n" +
            "• Good success is pursued through principles that please God.\n\n" +
            "• Integrity should never be sacrificed for temporary rewards.\n\n" +
            "• Wealth and recognition alone do not define a successful life.\n\n" +
            "• Joseph's example teaches the importance of remaining faithful under pressure.\n\n" +
            "• Our resources and abilities should be managed responsibly.\n\n" +
            "• Good success should also benefit and encourage others.\n\n" +
            "• God's Word should guide our ambitions and decisions.\n\n" +
            "• We should pursue success that honours God and preserves good character."
    );

    private Chapter02GoodSuccessAndBadSuccess() {
    }
      }
